      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The item assumes only “A commuting square of first maps between two standard cone triangles” in K(A), then asserts: “The square of chain maps induces the block-diagonal map of mapping cones.” Equality of the square in K(A) means bf and f'a are chain-homotopic, not necessarily equal as chain maps. The cited dependency thm-a-morphism-of-chain-maps-induces-a-chain-map-of-cones applies only to a strict square satisfying bf = ga. A homotopy correction in the cone map is required, and the block-diagonal map need not be a chain map.",
