      "location": "Proof 2.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The proof cites only the dependency statement “Cone(f[1]) ≅ Cone(f)[1]” and concludes that “the signed left rotation of the standard cone triangle is isomorphic ... to a standard cone triangle for the shifted map.” The rotated triangle has terms D → Cone(f) → C[1] → D[1], whereas the standard cone triangle of f[1] has terms C[1] → D[1] → Cone(f[1]) → C[2]. The displayed cone-shift isomorphism does not supply an isomorphism of these triangles. Establishing TR2 instead requires analysis of the cone of D → Cone(f), which is absent.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "2a90e5ab064ac9ccb9a938fc1658ae0ce89832a5781ca95d5b9a79612bdd6357"
    },
